        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 402.42,
          "end": 406.95,
          "en": "if they don't pick an answer before the timer expired.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 406.95,
          "end": 410.46,
          "en": "Therefore, instead of always outputting answer down there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 410.46,
          "end": 414.39,
          "en": "which could be null if no answer was picked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 414.39,
          "end": 417,
          "en": "because in that case in the quiz component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 417,
          "end": 421.59,
          "en": "we are storing null as a answer if the timer expired",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 421.59,
          "end": 423.183,
          "en": "and no answer was picked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 424.05,
          "end": 426.6,
          "en": "So therefore, instead of outputting null down there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 426.6,
          "end": 430.11,
          "en": "we should check if answer is truthy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 430.11,
          "end": 432.69,
          "en": "and as a fallback value if it's not,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 432.69,
          "end": 436.413,
          "en": "so if no answer was picked, we could output skipped here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 437.55,
          "end": 441.57,
          "en": "In addition, I wanna set this class name here conditionally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 441.57,
          "end": 444.96,
          "en": "to show the user on this screen here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 444.96,
          "end": 448.38,
          "en": "whether an answer is correct or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 448.38,
          "end": 452.28,
          "en": "To do that I'll dynamically derive the CSS class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 452.28,
          "end": 453.6,
          "en": "that should be added here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 453.6,
          "end": 456.84000000000003,
          "en": "for the answer we're currently looking at here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 456.84000000000003,
          "end": 460.02,
          "en": "And I'll add a CSS class variable for that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 460.02,
          "end": 463.38,
          "en": "which is always user-answer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 463.38,
          "end": 466.953,
          "en": "So that's the base CSS class that should always be added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 468.06,
          "end": 471.69,
          "en": "But then here we can check if answer is equal to null",
          "zh": ""
